take(): Efficiently retrieves a specified number of rows without loading the whole dataset into memory.

- The take() action is used to retrieve a specified number of records from the DataFrame or RDD without bringing the entire dataset to the driver.
- This makes it more memory-efficient compared to collect() for large datasets.

